{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-462090-r4615141","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Sambar III","sourcePageId":462090,"sourceRevision":"4615141","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:24:21Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Sambar%20III&oldid=4615141","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T14:15:46.048Z","sourceCategories":[],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"1a56eee9ce71a16b05f7e197ed3cb579b2915732ed9b69b0d8a5560d11b088bf","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Indian recipes\n| Servings = 5–6\n| Difficulty = 3\n}}\n\n{{Recipe}}\n\nThis recipe is a '''sambar''' variation. Served over steamed [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]], it makes for a simple but filling meal.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n=== Dahl ===\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] dry, split and hulled [[Cookbook:Lentil|red lentils]]\n* 3 cups [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Asafoetida|asafoetida]] (optional)\n\n=== Sambar ===\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Tamarind|tamarind]] pulp or 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] concentrate\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Ghee|ghee]], [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]] or [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Mustard|black or brown mustard seed]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Fenugreek|fenugreek seeds]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin seeds]]\n* 2–3 pinches of fresh or dry [[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|curry leaves]]\n* 2–3 [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] fresh or dry [[Cookbook:Chiles|chile peppers]] (choose variety suited to your palate)\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* 1–2 tsp chopped [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 1–2 tsp chopped or grated [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Cube|cubed]] [[Cookbook:Eggplant|eggplant]]\n* ½ cup cubed [[Cookbook:Potato|potato]]\n* ½ cup cubed [[Cookbook:Carrot|carrot]]\n* ½ cup cubed [[Cookbook:Daikon|daikon]]\n* ¼–1 tsp hot chile powder\n* 1 ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Sambar masalar|sambar masalar]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Green bean|green beans]] (optional)\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Drumstick|drumsticks]] (optional)\n* ¼ cup chopped [[Cookbook:Cilantro|cilantro]]\n* ½ cup cubed [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]]\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Bring the lentils and water to a [[Cookbook:Boiling|boil]]. Reduce heat, add salt and asafoetida, and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] until the lentils fall apart.\n# To prepare the tamarind pulp, mix the tamarind mass with twice the amount of water, then work with a fork to remove pits; later [[Cookbook:Straining|strain]] the pulp.\n# Heat the fat/oil in a pan. Add the mustard seeds, and heat until they pop.\n# Add fenugreek seeds, cumin seeds, curry leaves, chili peppers, and salt. [[Cookbook:Frying|Fry]] 1–2 minutes.\n# Add onions, and fry until glazed.\n# Add garlic, ginger, eggplant, potato, carrot, and daikon. Stir.\n# Move ingredients to side. Add chili powder to oil at the bottom of pot, then stir all.\n# Add sambar masalar, and stir.\n# Add 2 cups of water, and bring to boil. Reduce heat, and simmer 5–10 minutes.\n# Add tomato, green beans, and drumsticks, then simmer 5–10 minutes.\n# Add coriander, dhal (cooked lentils with their liquid), and tamarind. Simmer until vegetables are soft.\n# Serve hot over steamed rice.\n\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for curry]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tamarind]]\n[[Category:Recipes using asafoetida]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cilantro]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using white radish]]\n[[Category:Dal recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using eggplant]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fenugreek seed]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using red lentil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Sambar III","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"5–6","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 cup dry, split and hulled red lentils","sourceText":"1 cup dry, split and hulled red lentils","amountText":"1 cup dry, split and hulled red lentils","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"3 cups water","sourceText":"3 cups water","amountText":"3 cups water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"¼ tsp salt","sourceText":"¼ tsp salt","amountText":"¼ tsp salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"½ tsp asafoetida (optional)","sourceText":"½ tsp asafoetida (optional)","amountText":"½ tsp asafoetida (optional)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"½ cup tamarind pulp or 1 tbsp concentrate","sourceText":"½ cup tamarind pulp or 1 tbsp concentrate","amountText":"½ cup tamarind pulp or 1 tbsp concentrate","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"¼ cup ghee, butter or vegetable oil","sourceText":"¼ cup ghee, butter or vegetable oil","amountText":"¼ cup ghee, butter or vegetable oil","amount":null,"